{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (DOCTOR): Maureen, come on in. This computer is at me again, one second.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (CAREGIVER): That's no bother. The car park was a nightmare, mind. I'm Claire, her daughter. I live with her, and I do the pill box.",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (DOCTOR): Grand. What has you in?",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (CAREGIVER): Her ankles are up, and she's breathless just walking to the kitchen. About three weeks.",
  "[SEG0005] person_1 (DOCTOR): Sorry, say that again? The screen jumped on me.",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (CAREGIVER): Swollen ankles and short of breath. About three weeks.",
  "[SEG0007] person_1 (DOCTOR): Maureen, is the breathing the main thing?",
  "[SEG0008] person_3 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0009] person_1 (DOCTOR): Any pain in the chest?",
  "[SEG0010] person_3 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0011] person_1 (DOCTOR): Fever, or shivery?",
  "[SEG0012] person_3 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0013] person_2 (CAREGIVER): She is dog tired, mind. Asleep in the chair most afternoons.",
  "[SEG0014] person_1 (DOCTOR): How are you sleeping at night, Maureen?",
  "[SEG0015] person_3 (PATIENT): Grand.",
  "[SEG0016] person_1 (DOCTOR): Is the breath worse lying down?",
  "[SEG0017] person_2 (CAREGIVER): A small bit. She's on an extra pillow this past fortnight.",
  "[SEG0018] person_3 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0019] person_1 (DOCTOR): Both ankles, or just the one?",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (CAREGIVER): Both. Worse by evening, and the shoes won't go on.",
  "[SEG0021] person_1 (DOCTOR): Any cough with it?",
  "[SEG0022] person_3 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0023] person_1 (DOCTOR): Right. The medication list on here looks messy. Claire, what's she actually taking?",
  "[SEG0024] person_2 (CAREGIVER): The water tablet in the morning. Furosemide, 40 milligrams, once a day, for the fluid.",
  "[SEG0025] person_1 (DOCTOR): 40 milligrams. Say the other ones again, I clicked off it.",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (CAREGIVER): The little white one is ramipril, 5 milligrams, meant to be one in the morning for the blood pressure.",
  "[SEG0027] person_1 (DOCTOR): Only the morning?",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (CAREGIVER): That's what was intended. But, well, actually I double-counted it filling the box. There's another little white one in the evening slot, the same tablet. I only copped it yesterday.",
  "[SEG0029] person_1 (DOCTOR): Maureen, morning and night for the white one?",
  "[SEG0030] person_3 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0031] person_2 (CAREGIVER): So this past week she may have been getting 10 milligrams, not the 5. Um, it's not a separate tablet.",
  "[SEG0032] person_1 (DOCTOR): Anything else?",
  "[SEG0033] person_2 (CAREGIVER): The other doctor stopped the amlodipine in March. Five milligrams. She hasn't taken it since.",
  "[SEG0034] person_3 (PATIENT): Stopped.",
  "[SEG0035] person_1 (DOCTOR): And the atorvastatin that was written up?",
  "[SEG0036] person_2 (CAREGIVER): She never took that. Not one tablet. The box is still sealed in the press.",
  "[SEG0037] person_1 (DOCTOR): We leave that out so. Any drug allergies?",
  "[SEG0038] person_3 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0039] person_2 (CAREGIVER): None.",
  "[SEG0040] person_1 (DOCTOR): Do you smoke, Maureen?",
  "[SEG0041] person_3 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0042] person_1 (DOCTOR): Arm out. Blood pressure is 108 over 64. Pulse is 58.",
  "[SEG0043] person_1 (DOCTOR): Any light-headedness?",
  "[SEG0044] person_3 (PATIENT): Sometimes.",
  "[SEG0045] person_2 (CAREGIVER): When she stands up, this last week.",
  "[SEG0046] person_1 (DOCTOR): I'll have a listen to the chest. Big breath.",
  "[SEG0047] person_1 (DOCTOR): Lungs are clear, no crackles. Heart sounds regular. Both ankles pit, and it goes up to the shins.",
  "[SEG0048] person_1 (DOCTOR): I'd say it's fluid in the legs, and the dizziness is from the ramipril being taken twice. Lungs are clear so I'm not calling a bad flare.",
  "[SEG0049] person_1 (DOCTOR): I'll push the water tablet up to 80 milligrams every morning.",
  "[SEG0050] person_2 (CAREGIVER): Doctor, the pressure is only 108, and she's been dizzy.",
  "[SEG0051] person_1 (DOCTOR): Ah, you're right. Scratch the 80. We'll leave the furosemide at 40 milligrams, once every morning. No increase.",
  "[SEG0052] person_1 (DOCTOR): What I'll change is the ramipril, down to 2.5 milligrams, once in the morning only. No tablet at night.",
  "[SEG0053] person_2 (CAREGIVER): I'll clear the evening slot out of the box.",
  "[SEG0054] person_1 (DOCTOR): Do that. And bring the spare bottle back to the chemist so it doesn't get taken again.",
  "[SEG0055] person_3 (PATIENT): Grand.",
  "[SEG0056] person_1 (DOCTOR): I want bloods this week, the kidney function and the salts. The form will be at reception. I was going to add a chest x-ray, but no, actually we'll not. Chest is clear and we'll watch it.",
  "[SEG0057] person_2 (CAREGIVER): Do you want her back?",
  "[SEG0058] person_1 (DOCTOR): Book her in a fortnight. Sooner if the breathing worsens or she faints, mind."
 ],
